WEBVTT

00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:09.080
In the Lahti Venture Program at LUT University, student teams from different disciplines solve a real problem for a real company.

00:00:09.080 --> 00:00:10.260
I am their mentor.

00:00:10.760 --> 00:00:15.500
Our company was Kempower, a Finnish maker of electric vehicle chargers.

00:00:15.500 --> 00:00:20.430
The challenge: how can Kempower attract and keep talent from Generation Z?

00:00:20.930 --> 00:00:23.190
I did not hand the team a framework.

00:00:23.190 --> 00:00:28.230
They were Generation Z themselves, so I asked what they expect from an employer.

00:00:28.230 --> 00:00:31.130
Their own answers became the first hypothesis.

00:00:31.630 --> 00:00:33.870
Then the team planned its evidence.

00:00:33.870 --> 00:00:37.790
Surveys and interviews with students and young professionals.

00:00:37.790 --> 00:00:40.670
A comparison with other technology companies.

00:00:40.670 --> 00:00:43.370
An analysis of themes, strengths and gaps.

00:00:43.370 --> 00:00:48.310
And finally a proposal: an employer value proposition built for Generation Z.

00:00:48.810 --> 00:00:54.030
Purpose, growth, flexibility and openness came through as the themes that matter.

00:00:54.030 --> 00:00:59.650
And a company working on clean transport has a real story to tell on the first of them.

00:01:00.150 --> 00:01:02.430
The ideas belonged to the students.

00:01:02.430 --> 00:01:07.970
My part was to ask, to structure, and to protect the space in which ideas can appear.

